From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:37:43 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sdm845: add tertiary MI2S support

The comma 3X records its microphones on TERTIARY_MI2S_TX, with the SoC
as bit clock and frame master, but the sdm845 machine driver only
handles the primary, secondary and quaternary MI2S ports and rejects
the tertiary one with "invalid dai id".

Handle TERTIARY_MI2S_RX/TX like the secondary port: enable the
tertiary MI2S bit clock at 1.536 MHz on the first stream, release it on
the last one, make the CPU DAI the bit clock and frame master, and set
the codec DAI to I2S format.

Based on Trey Moen's vamOS PR 128.

[adeeb: split from the amplifier MCLK change, rebase on v7.3]
Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c
index cc8452474f..3cc53cd4eb 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ struct sdm845_snd_data {
 	bool stream_prepared[AFE_PORT_MAX];
 	uint32_t pri_mi2s_clk_count;
 	uint32_t sec_mi2s_clk_count;
+	uint32_t ter_mi2s_clk_count;
 	uint32_t quat_tdm_clk_count;
 };
 
@@ -212,6 +213,8 @@ static int sdm845_snd_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 	case QUATERNARY_MI2S_RX:
 	case SECONDARY_MI2S_RX:
 	case SECONDARY_MI2S_TX:
+	case TERTIARY_MI2S_RX:
+	case TERTIARY_MI2S_TX:
 		break;
 	default:
 		pr_err("%s: invalid dai id 0x%x\n", __func__, cpu_dai->id);
@@ -364,6 +367,18 @@ static int sdm845_snd_startup(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 		snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(cpu_dai, fmt);
 		snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(codec_dai, codec_dai_fmt);
 		break;
+
+	case TERTIARY_MI2S_RX:
+	case TERTIARY_MI2S_TX:
+		codec_dai_fmt |= SND_SOC_DAIFMT_NB_NF | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S;
+		if (++(data->ter_mi2s_clk_count) == 1) {
+			snd_soc_dai_set_sysclk(cpu_dai,
+				Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_TER_MI2S_IBIT,
+				MI2S_BCLK_RATE,	SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE);
+		}
+		snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(cpu_dai, fmt);
+		snd_soc_dai_set_fmt(codec_dai, codec_dai_fmt);
+		break;
 	case QUATERNARY_MI2S_RX:
 		codec_dai_fmt |= SND_SOC_DAIFMT_NB_NF | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_I2S;
 		snd_soc_dai_set_sysclk(cpu_dai,
@@ -447,6 +462,15 @@ static void  sdm845_snd_shutdown(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 		}
 		break;
 
+	case TERTIARY_MI2S_RX:
+	case TERTIARY_MI2S_TX:
+		if (--(data->ter_mi2s_clk_count) == 0) {
+			snd_soc_dai_set_sysclk(cpu_dai,
+				Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_TER_MI2S_IBIT,
+				0, SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE);
+		}
+		break;
+
 	case QUATERNARY_TDM_RX_0:
 	case QUATERNARY_TDM_TX_0:
 		if (--(data->quat_tdm_clk_count) == 0) {
